{{also|coïncide|coïncidé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|coïncider}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|coincīdēre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|coincīdō}}, from {{m|la|co-}} + {{m|la|incīdō}}, from {{m|la|in-}} + {{m|la|cadō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-coincide.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪd|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|coincid}}

# To occupy exactly the same [[space]].
#: ''The two squares '''coincide''' nicely.''
# To occur at the same time.
#: ''The conference will '''coincide''' with his vacation.''
# To [[correspond]], [[concur]], or [[agree]].
#: ''Our ideas '''coincide''', except in certain areas.''

